Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: ONE workshop equipment design board for DUST RUSH, a polished stylized monstertruck game.
Show six independent believable workshop asset groups in a spacious 3 by 2 grid, equal visual weighting, consistent front-three-quarter angle, fully in frame:
1 a chunky orange rolling tool cabinet with metal handles, seven drawers, black rubber casters, a folded gray cloth on top;
2 a sturdy timber-topped steel workbench with a small bench vise and an attached tidy wall pegboard carrying individually recognizable spanners, pliers and screwdrivers;
3 a REAL low hydraulic floor jack with twin front roller wheels, rear casters, a long angled black handle and a hinged lifting arm terminating in a round black lifting pad. Its body is elongated and low, NOT a broom or lever stuck in a cube;
4 a small turquoise horizontal cylinder air compressor on two black wheels with motor housing, pressure gauge and neatly coiled orange hose;
5 a broad low steel service/lift platform scaled for a monstertruck, orange painted safety edges and sturdy angled ramps at each end;
6 a steel rack holding three spare deep-tread monstertruck wheels with orange beadlock rims, with an overhead industrial strip-light fixture resting above it as a separated small companion prop.
Art direction: premium stylized-realistic 3D racing-game asset design, rounded manufactured edges, rich readable surfaces, subtle wear, orange enamel, turquoise enamel, graphite steel, brushed metal, satin rubber and warm wood. Moderate achievable mechanical detail, strong silhouettes recognizable without text by a child. Same visual language as glossy turquoise/orange monstertruck concept art.
Background: fully OPAQUE continuous warm ivory studio background, neutral softbox lighting with soft neutral grounded shadows. No alpha cutouts, no red/yellow fringes. No words, labels, logos, watermark, people or complete vehicles.
